{"reviews":[{"id":"B009AQK8CK-0","r":5.0,"t":"Yay","x":"My 5 year old son  loves them, even though he doesn't need them. Baba Booey Baba Booey Baba Booey Fafa Fooey","h":7,"v":1,"d":"May 2014"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-1","r":5.0,"t":"A good fit for a child","x":"5 stars or as my 9 year old son says &#34;five eyes&#34;.  He loves these glasses and will be using them for a cosplay party where he is playing the Vocaloid, Kiyoteru. I think that the plastic causes a bit of blur.  He says &#34;Thank you Amazon&#34;.","h":4,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-2","r":5.0,"t":"Very cute!","x":"Santa brought these for my daughter after her siblings needed glasses and she didn't. She was disappointed and wanted glasses of her own. So, Santa brought these in a cute little eyeglass case he found at Bed Bath and Beyond. She LOVES them. Very cute.","h":4,"v":1,"d":"Dec 2013"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-3","r":5.0,"t":"Grandsons loved them","x":"MY GRANDSONS ARE ALWAYS PUTTING MY GLASSES ON SO I BOUGHT THESE SO THEY CAN WEAR THEIR OWN GLASSES. THEY LOVE THEM.","h":4,"v":1,"d":"Apr 2014"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-4","r":5.0,"t":"Perfect for Clark Kent on his 1st birthday","x":"Perfect for Clark Kent on his 1st birthday.  Still oversized for a baby but not adult-sized so they fall off.","h":4,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-5","r":5.0,"t":"Great fake glasses for kids to play with!","x":"My 10 yr old son wears eyeglasses and my 4 yr old daughter wants to be just like her bubba. I bought these fake plastic glasses for her to wear to be like her brother without messing up her vision. She loves them!! They're great for the cheap price that they are!","h":3,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2014"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-6","r":5.0,"t":"Five Stars","x":"Perfect &#34;fake&#34; glasses for my daughter's mock trial outfit.  She's 7 and they worked out really well.","h":3,"v":1,"d":"Jun 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-7","r":5.0,"t":"Very satisfied","x":"My son absolutely loves the glasses and wears them all the time. He is 6 years old and wants to wear glasses like his older brother.  I didn't want to spend a ton on non-prescriptive glasses that he would probably lose or break.  These are perfect and can't beat the price.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Mar 2016"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-8","r":5.0,"t":"Great costume glasses for kids","x":"Great costume glasses for kids.  Son had to dress up for 100 day of school as an old man.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-9","r":5.0,"t":"Five Stars","x":"My granddaughter has multiple pairs of these and wears them daily.","h":2,"v":1,"d":"Dec 2014"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-10","r":5.0,"t":"Five Stars","x":"Granddaughter loves them for s***s and giggles ;)","h":2,"v":1,"d":"May 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-11","r":4.0,"t":"Good for protective eye wear or decorative wear for kids","x":"These fake glasses have a plain lens which is heavy plastic, not glass.  I looked through them to make sure they were plain (and wouldn't hurt my kids' eyes).  They remind me of plexiglass.  We purchased to use solely during spring allergy season to keep pollen out of my children's eyes (they are highly sensitive and need something every time they leave the house).  The glasses serve their purpose.  They are cheap, so I don't know how long they'll last.  They look a little too big on my 10 year ","h":1,"v":1,"d":"May 2014"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-12","r":3.0,"t":"They will do their job as \"glasses\" for the little ...","x":"They will do their job as &#34;glasses&#34; for the little sister while the big sister has real ones. They are cheaply made though and I expect the pins to fall out soon.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Sep 2014"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-13","r":5.0,"t":"and they were perfect! My daughter loves them","x":"It is so hard to find kids' sized play glasses, so I was excited to find these in the nick of time. Shipped quickly, and they were perfect! My daughter loves them.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Nov 2016"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-14","r":5.0,"t":"Great for kids","x":"Perfect for my son!  I wear glasses and my four year old felt left out.  I got these for him and they fit him perfectly and look adorable.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Apr 2016"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-15","r":3.0,"t":"Used them for my son's 100th Day of School costume ...","x":"Used them for my son's 100th Day of School costume. Lens popped out but was able to pop it back in.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-16","r":2.0,"t":"Not kid sized","x":"These are adult sized glasses. I ended up throwing them away.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-17","r":3.0,"t":"Three Stars","x":"We love the realistic look, but the lens keeps popping out.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-18","r":4.0,"t":"my great grand daughter loves them","x":"Child's present, my great grand daughter loves them.","h":1,"v":1,"d":"Dec 2014"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-19","r":3.0,"t":"Super Cute But Not Able To Hang Out With Kids","x":"My twin boys are 7 and they both like the look of wearing glasses but don't need corrective lenses.  I bought them each a pair of these, not expecting miracles.  No miracles, no disappointment there. Kids aren't expected to gentle on things so I didn't figure they would last terribly long but given they are designed for children, at least the lenght of wear they get out of dollar store sunglasses would be appreciated. Our experience with these glasses was a few days, or less, for both pairs.  Th","h":0,"v":1,"d":"Aug 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-20","r":2.0,"t":"My grandson always want to wear our reading glasses, ...","x":"My grandson always want to wear our reading glasses, so we thought these would be just the ticket for him to play with.  The first day with very limited use the right lens on both pairs fell out of the frames.  Must be a defect.  I had to superglue the lens to the frame.","h":0,"v":1,"d":"Feb 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-21","r":3.0,"t":"Fun but cheap","x":"My daughter was always trying on my parents glasses I didn't want her to ruin her eyes so I bought these. They fit good buy broke pretty soon. We still play with them every now and than even tho the frame broke. I'd still recommend them they were fun","h":0,"v":1,"d":"Jul 2016"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-22","r":2.0,"t":"Very fragile. break easily","x":"Very fragile.  I bought these for my 3 year old son because he wanted to wear glasses. I thought they were an excellent choice even after I had them in my hands.  They were broken into pieces within 24 hours.","h":0,"v":1,"d":"Aug 2015"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-23","r":5.0,"t":"Worked out great","x":"My 7 year old grandson loves them.  He wanted glasses and I think this is his favorite gift out of everything he got.  I'm sure they won't last forever but for the price, you can't beat them.","h":0,"v":1,"d":"Apr 2014"},{"id":"B009AQK8CK-24","r":5.0,"t":"These are cute and a good price. My daughter is 8 and obsessed with ...","x":"These are cute and a good price. My daughter is 8 and obsessed with fake glasses. I wear glasses and she wants to wear them and look like me. She loves them.","h":0,"v":1,"d":"Dec 2015"}],"emb":"","summary":{"claims":[{"text":"Reviewers frequently say children love these glasses and wear them often, especially kids who want to imitate a sibling or parent who wears real glasses.","cites":[1,2,3,4,6,8,10,11,14,15]},{"text":"Many buyers praise the low price and good value for non-prescription play glasses.","cites":[6,8,13]},{"text":"Several reviewers note the glasses fit children well, though some mention they are oversized for babies or toddlers.","cites":[2,5,15]},{"text":"A few reviewers mention the plastic lenses or construction cause blur or feel cheaply made.","cites":[2,12,13]},{"text":"Reviewers commonly use these as costume or dress-up glasses for parties, school events, and cosplay.","cites":[2,7,9]}]},"qa":[]}